***
*** test_ordering.maude
***
*** Layered test suite for the belief/estPos ordering fix.
***
*** METHOD: each layer is built ONLY from values produced by earlier layers.
*** Nobody has to guess an expected answer: a later test is correct iff it
*** equals a function of earlier printed outputs. Where a value is fully
*** determined by arithmetic, it is written in the comment as [EXPECT ...].
*** Where it depends on YOUR definition of projectBelief, it is written as
*** [DERIVE: ...] and must be checked against the earlier printed value.
***
*** RUN WITH:   maude load_all.maude test_ordering.maude
*** (or: load load_all.maude   then   load test_ordering.maude)
***

load load_all.maude

***
*** test_ordering.maude
***
*** Layered test suite for the belief/estPos ordering fix.
***
*** METHOD: each layer is built ONLY from values produced by earlier layers.
*** Nobody has to guess an expected answer: a later test is correct iff it
*** equals a function of earlier printed outputs. Where a value is fully
*** determined by arithmetic, it is written in the comment as [EXPECT ...].
*** Where it depends on YOUR definition of projectBelief, it is written as
*** [DERIVE: ...] and must be checked against the earlier printed value.
***
*** RUN WITH:   maude load_all.maude test_ordering.maude
*** (or: load load_all.maude   then   load test_ordering.maude)
***

load load_all.maude

***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 0 - PRIMITIVES  (anchors: pure arithmetic, no model semantics)
*** =====================================================================
*** If any of these is wrong, nothing below is meaningful.
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L0 primitives ==" .

*** L0.1  [EXPECT 1]  period must be 1, every later projection assumes it
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : period .

*** L0.2  [EXPECT 50]
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : distSq(v(0,0,0), v(5,5,0)) .

*** L0.3  [EXPECT 18]
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : distSq(v(0,0,0), v(3,3,0)) .

*** L0.4  [EXPECT false]  50 > 25, so the two drones in example.maude
***       start OUT of range. Cross-checked by L6.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : inCommunicationRange(v(0,0,0), v(5,5,0)) .

*** L0.5  [EXPECT true]   18 <= 25
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : inCommunicationRange(v(0,0,0), v(3,3,0)) .

*** L0.6  [EXPECT true]   distSq = 0 <= 64  (centre of the reliable zone)
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : hasReliablePerception(v(15,15,15)) .

*** L0.7  [EXPECT false]  distSq = 75 > 64
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : hasReliablePerception(v(20,20,20)) .

*** L0.8  [EXPECT v(6/10,6/10,6/10)]
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : dirToVec(NEU) .

*** L0.9  [EXPECT NEU]  pure diagonal goal => diagonal-up heading.
***       Used as the expected heading in L2/L3.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : bestDir(v(20,20,20), v(40,40,40)) .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 1 - THE TWO BELIEF FUNCTIONS, IN ISOLATION
*** =====================================================================
*** This layer exists to answer ONE question: does belief now decay
*** once per round, or twice? L1.1 is the decay inside calcBelief that
*** was already in fusion_logic.maude. L1.2 is the new projectBelief.
*** L1.3 is their composition = exactly what think/ should produce.
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L1 belief functions ==" .

*** L1.1  [EXPECT 49/50]  empty inbox => W=0 < trustThreshold(1)
***       => else-branch => B - 1/50 = 1 - 1/50
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : calcBelief(1/1, v(20,20,20), none) .

*** L1.2  [DERIVE] projectBelief applied to the SAME input as L1.1.
***       If this returns 49/50 too, projectBelief decays by 1/50.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : projectBelief(1/1, period) .

*** L1.3  [DERIVE = projectBelief(L1.1)] the composition think/ performs.
***       *** DIAGNOSTIC ***
***       If L1.3 == L1.1  -> projectBelief is the identity, single decay.
***       If L1.3 <  L1.1  -> DOUBLE DECAY: calcBelief and projectBelief
***                           are both shrinking belief in one round.
***       Compare against L2.2 which must be identical.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : projectBelief(calcBelief(1/1, v(20,20,20), none), period) .

*** L1.4  boundary probe. muLost(1/2)=0 and muConfident(1/2)=0, so the
***       empty-inbox branch of evalSpeedSet divides 0 by 0.
***       [EXPECT: an un-reduced term / error, NOT a number]
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : evalSpeedSet(v(0,0,0), E, 1/2, none) .

*** L1.5  [EXPECT 1]  sanity: high belief, no neighbours => full cruise.
***       Used as expected speed in L2.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : evalSpeedSet(v(20,20,20), NEU, 49/50, none) .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 2 - think/ ON ONE DRONE, NO INBOX, OUTSIDE PERCEPTION ZONE
*** =====================================================================
*** Everything here is predicted by L0+L1:
***   FUSED-EP = calcEstPos(EP,B,none) = EP          (W=0 < threshold)
***   FUSED-B  = L1.1
***   NEW-H    = L0.9  = NEU
***   NEW-S    = L1.5  = 1
***   PROJ-EP  = EP + dirToVec(NEU)*1  = v(103/5,103/5,103/5)
***   PROJ-B   = L1.3
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L2 think, isolated ==" .

*** L2.1 full object. Check each attribute against the predictions above.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  think(< d(1) : Drone | pos : v(20,20,20), estPos : v(20,20,20),
                          goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                          speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >) .

*** L2.2  [MUST EQUAL L1.3]  the belief attribute alone, recomputed.
***       If L2.1's belief differs from L1.3, think/ is not composing
***       calcBelief and projectBelief the way the fix intends.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : projectBelief(calcBelief(1/1, v(20,20,20), none), period) .

*** L2.3  [MUST EQUAL L2.1's estPos]  independent recomputation of PROJ-EP.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : estimateNextPosition(v(20,20,20), 1/1, NEU, period) .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 3 - applyPhysics MUST NOW TOUCH ONLY pos
*** =====================================================================
*** estPos is deliberately set to a value think/ would never produce
*** v(9,9,9)) so that any change to it is visible immediately.
***   pos' = v(0,0,0) + dirToVec(E)*1 + wind*1 = v(1,1/10,0)
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L3 applyPhysics ==" .

*** L3.1  [EXPECT pos = v(1,1/10,0), estPos = v(9,9,9) UNCHANGED,
***               belief = 1 UNCHANGED]
***       If estPos moved, the old estimateNextPosition line is still in
***       applyPhysicsAcc and is overwriting think/'s result.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  applyPhysics(< d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(9,9,9),
                                 goalPos : v(1,1,1), belief : 1/1,
                                 speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >,
               wind(v(0,1/10,0))) .

*** L3.2  [EXPECT v(1,1/10,0)]  independent recomputation of pos'.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : updatePhysicalState(v(0,0,0), 1/1, E, wind(v(0,1/10,0)), period) .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 4 - ONE WHOLE SYNCHRONOUS STEP
*** =====================================================================
*** A single drone, no neighbours, outside the perception zone, so the
*** step reduces to: think (L2) then applyPhysics-on-pos (L3).
*** The result must be reconstructible from L2 and L3 by hand:
***   estPos, belief, speed, heading  <- exactly L2.1
***   pos                             <- L3-style update of v(20,20,20)
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L4 one full step ==" .

*** L4.1 one rewrite = one performSyncStep.
***      [CROSS-CHECK] its estPos/belief/heading/speed must match L2.1.
rew [1] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(20,20,20), estPos : v(20,20,20),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none > } .

*** L4.2 two steps. estPos should advance by dirToVec(NEU) again, and
***      belief should drop by exactly the SAME amount it dropped in L4.1.
***      [DIAGNOSTIC] a per-step belief drop of 2/50 here versus 1/50
***      expected from L1.1 alone confirms the double decay.
rew [2] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(20,20,20), estPos : v(20,20,20),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none > } .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 5 - PERCEPTION OVERRIDE
*** =====================================================================
*** Drone sits at the centre of the reliable zone with a badly wrong
*** estPos and a low belief. The override in think/ must discard both.
***   FUSED-EP = pos = v(15,15,15)     (NOT fused with v(30,30,30))
***   FUSED-B  = 1
***   PROJ-B   = projectBelief(1, 1)   = L1.2
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L5 perception override ==" .

*** L5.1  [EXPECT estPos to be v(15,15,15) + dirToVec(bestDir) ,
***               i.e. derived from pos, with NO trace of v(30,30,30)]
***       [EXPECT belief == L1.2]
***       If belief here is 1, projectBelief is identity.
***       If belief here is < 1, a perfect GPS fix still loses confidence
***       in the same round it was acquired - report this, it is a
***       modelling decision that needs to be deliberate.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  think(< d(1) : Drone | pos : v(15,15,15), estPos : v(30,30,30),
                          goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/10,
                          speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >) .

*** L5.2 the same drone through a whole step, with perceiveEnvironment
***      in front of it. Must agree with L5.1 on estPos/belief.
***      [CROSS-CHECK] if L5.1 and L5.2 disagree, perceiveEnvironment and
***      the in-think override are fighting each other.
rew [1] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(15,15,15), estPos : v(30,30,30),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/10,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none > } .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 6 - FUSION ACTUALLY FIRING
*** =====================================================================
*** L0.4 showed v(0,0,0)/v(5,5,0) are NOT in range, so those two never
*** fuse on round 1. Here they are placed at distSq = 18 (in range) so
*** WCL runs. Both have belief 1, so W = 1 >= trustThreshold.
***   calcEstPos = ((EP*1) + (V*1)) / (1+1) = midpoint
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L6 fusion ==" .

*** L6.1  [EXPECT the midpoint of v(0,0,0) and v(3,3,0) = v(3/2,3/2,0)]
***       pure WCL check, no drones involved.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : calcEstPos(v(0,0,0), 1/1, msg(d(2), v(3,3,0), 1/1)) .

*** L6.2  [EXPECT reinforcement, not decay: W >= 1 so belief goes UP,
***       capped at 1. distSq(v(0,0,0),v(3,3,0)) = 18 > 4, so the
***       sumBeliefWeights discount of 1/2 applies => W = 1/2.
***       1/2 < trustThreshold(1) => actually the DECAY branch fires.]
***       *** This mismatch between calcEstPos's W (=1, undiscounted)
***       *** and calcBelief's W (=1/2, discounted) is worth noting:
***       *** position fuses but belief simultaneously decays.
red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : calcBelief(1/1, v(0,0,0), msg(d(2), v(3,3,0), 1/1)) .

*** L6.3 two drones IN range, one full step. Round 1 has empty inboxes
***      nothing has been broadcast yet), so round 1 must equal the
***      no-neighbour case; fusion can only appear from round 2.
***      [CROSS-CHECK] compare round-1 belief here with L4.1's.
rew [1] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(0,0,0), goalPos : v(20,20,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
    < d(2) : Drone | pos : v(3,3,0), estPos : v(3,3,0), goalPos : v(20,29,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none > } .

*** L6.4 three steps: by now messages have flowed and WCL has fired.
***      Check estPos values have been pulled toward each other relative
***      to what pure dead-reckoning (L2.3-style) would give.
rew [3] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(0,0,0), goalPos : v(20,20,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
    < d(2) : Drone | pos : v(3,3,0), estPos : v(3,3,0), goalPos : v(20,29,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none > } .


***
*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 7 - INVARIANTS VIA SEARCH  (the real regression tests)
*** =====================================================================
*** These are the ones that must not silently change when the ordering
*** is edited again later.
***

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== L7 invariants ==" .

*** L7.1 BELIEF STAYS IN RANGE.
***      Belief is specified as a value in [0,1]. Look for any reachable
***      state violating that.
***      [EXPECT: No solution]
***      A solution here means a decay/reinforce path drives belief out
***      of its own domain - a hard bug, independent of ordering.
search [1, 12] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(20,20,20), estPos : v(20,20,20),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ < d(1) : Drone | belief : B:Rat, AS:AttributeSet > | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that B:Rat < 0/1 or B:Rat > 1/1 .

*** L7.2 EPISTEMIC DRIFT IS BOUNDED WHILE ALONE.
***      One drone, no neighbours, wind pushing it around. estPos is pure
***      dead-reckoning so the gap grows by at most |wind|*period = 1/10
***      per round. Over 10 rounds distSq(pos,estPos) <= (10*1/10)^2 = 1.
***      [EXPECT: No solution]  If this finds a state, the gap is growing
***      faster than the wind can explain => estPos is being updated
***      somewhere it should not be (i.e. twice).
search [1, 10] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(20,20,20), estPos : v(20,20,20),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ < d(1) : Drone | pos : P:loc, estPos : EP:loc, AS:AttributeSet > | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that distSq(P:loc, EP:loc) > 1/1 .

*** L7.3 PERCEPTION IS A FIXED POINT.
***      A drone parked inside the reliable zone (goal = its own position,
***      so bestDir should pick stop and it never leaves) must never let
***      its estimate drift far from pos: it is re-anchored every round.
***      [EXPECT: No solution]
search [1, 10] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(15,15,15), estPos : v(15,15,15),
                      goalPos : v(15,15,15), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ < d(1) : Drone | pos : P:loc, estPos : EP:loc, AS:AttributeSet > | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that distSq(P:loc, EP:loc) > 1/1 .

*** L7.4 THE PAPER'S OWN QUERY, SHORT HORIZON.
***      Paper says: fails at 10, succeeds at 15.
***      [EXPECT: a solution]  (mission NOT yet accomplished at N=10)
search [1, 10] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(30,30,30), estPos : v(30,30,30),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ C:Configuration | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that N:Nat >= 10 and not metaObjectiveAccomplished(C:Configuration, IC:Nat) .

*** L7.5 SAME QUERY, LONGER HORIZON.
***      [EXPECT: No solution]  If L7.4 gives a solution and L7.5 does
***      not, the paper's claim survives the ordering fix unchanged.
***      If BOTH give solutions, the fix slowed the drone down - most
***      likely because belief now decays twice and the fuzzy controller
***      is throttling speed. That is the single most informative pair
***      of results in this file.
search [1, 15] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(30,30,30), estPos : v(30,30,30),
                      goalPos : v(40,40,40), belief : 1/1,
                      speed : 1/1, heading : E, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ C:Configuration | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that N:Nat >= 15 and not metaObjectiveAccomplished(C:Configuration, IC:Nat) .

*** L7.6 NO CRASHES between two converging drones.
***      [EXPECT: No solution] if the fuzzy controller does its job.
***      countDrones is used (countAgents in example.maude does not exist
***      in the uploaded modules - that query would not have parsed).
search [1, 12] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(0,0,0), goalPos : v(20,20,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
    < d(2) : Drone | pos : v(3,3,0), estPos : v(3,3,0), goalPos : v(20,29,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ C:Configuration | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that countDrones(C:Configuration) < IC:Nat .

*** L7.7 EPISTEMIC SUCCESS THRESHOLD (the paper's section 5.3 query).
***      [EXPECT: No solution] at this horizon per the paper.
search [1, 15] in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS :
  initAnalysis(
    < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(0,0,0), goalPos : v(20,20,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
    < d(2) : Drone | pos : v(5,5,0), estPos : v(5,5,0), goalPos : v(20,29,0),
                      belief : 1/1, speed : 1/1, heading : NE, inbox : none >
  )
  =>* [ C:Configuration | N:Nat, IC:Nat ]
  such that meanEpistemicSuccess(C:Configuration, IC:Nat) < 7/10 .

*** =====================================================================
*** LAYER 8 - COLLISION FORECAST COVERS THE WHOLE PERIOD [0,1]
*** =====================================================================
*** Unclamped CPA time here is 11/10 > 1, but at t = 1 the drones are
*** 1/10 apart (distSq 1/100 <= crashThresholdSq). Pre-fix this returned 2
*** = no crash.
*** L8.1  [EXPECT 1]  crash detected at the end of the period
red in SWARM-ANALYSIS : checkSweptCollision(v(0,0,0), v(1/2,0,0), v(11/10,0,0), v(-1/2,0,0)) .

*** L8.2  INVARIANT: no two surviving drones are ever within crashThresholdSq.
***       Pre-fix: Solution (state 15, all-updraft path; the pair is 0.3
***       apart at the end of round 3 and never removed).
***       [EXPECT: No solution]
search [1, 3] in SWARM-ANALYSIS :
  { < d(1) : Drone | pos : v(0,0,0), estPos : v(0,0,0), goalPos : v(9/10,-17/10,0),
                      belief : 1, speed : 0, heading : stop, inbox : none >
    < d(2) : Drone | pos : v(21/10,0,0), estPos : v(21/10,0,0), goalPos : v(1/5,-14/5,2/5),
                      belief : 1, speed : 0, heading : stop, inbox : none > }
  =>* { < d(1) : Drone | pos : P1:loc, AS1:AttributeSet >
        < d(2) : Drone | pos : P2:loc, AS2:AttributeSet > }
  such that distSq(P1:loc, P2:loc) <= crashThresholdSq .

red in SWARM-META-ANALYSIS : "== done ==" .